cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "openalex-semantic-search: semantic search over 300M+ OpenAlex works: GPU-embedded, served from one CPU server"
abstract: >-
  Dense retrieval over 300 million plus OpenAlex scholarly records without a vector
  database. A one-off GPU batch job embeds the corpus with BGE-small; a single CPU
  server builds a FAISS IVF-PQ index, re-scores candidates with INT8 vectors, merges
  exact and prefix title matches, and serves queries through an HTTP API.
authors:
  - family-names: Prabhulal
    given-names: Arjun
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/arjunprabhulal/openalex-semantic-search"
url: "https://arjunprabhulal.com/how-i-built-semantic-search-300m-academic-papers/"
keywords:
  - semantic search
  - dense retrieval
  - OpenAlex
  - FAISS
  - product quantization
  - INT8 quantization
  - scholarly search
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-27"
